---
import { sitePath } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { LAB_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Our Lab" description={`About the ${LAB_NAME} at Tufts University.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap lab-page">
      <h1>About Our Lab</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The {LAB_NAME}, in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Tufts
        University, studies how climate extremes affect earthen infrastructure and the communities
        it serves.
      </p>

      <h2>Challenge</h2>
      <p>
        Drought, flooding, and wildfire change soil moisture and temperature, and with them soil
        strength and deformation. These changes can reduce the stability of slopes, dams, and
        levees. Compound and cascading hazards, in which events overlap or follow one another, add
        to this risk. When these structures fail, the consequences reach the communities that
        depend on them.
      </p>

      <h2>Contribution</h2>
      <p>
        Our work focuses on critical infrastructure such as levees and dams: how it withstands
        extreme events in a changing climate, and how it can be adapted. We pair geotechnical
        engineering with environmental justice, paying particular attention to the risks facing
        disadvantaged communities.
      </p>

      <h2>Approach</h2>
      <p>
        We use analytical and numerical methods to study water flow, heat transfer, and stress
        in variably saturated soils. We apply these models to slopes, dams, and levees under
        changing climate conditions. Much of this work is collaborative, drawing on climate
        science, hydrology, geosciences, social science, remote sensing, and data science.
      </p>

      <p class="about-actions">
        The lab is led by <a href={sitePath('/about')}>Prof. Farshid Vahedifard</a>. Our
        <a href={sitePath('/projects')}>projects</a> and
        <a href={sitePath('/publications')}>publications</a> describe this work in more detail, and
        we welcome <a href={sitePath('/join')}>inquiries</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
